.TH DIPISRT 1 "2026-08-22" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipisrt \- bridge a DVB-IPI stream between RTP/UDP/file and an SRT link, sender or receiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipisrt
.B \-i
.I uri
.B \-o
.I uri
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipisrt
bridges a DVB-IPI stream between a plain RTP/UDP/file endpoint and an SRT
link, in either direction, using libsrt. SRT is not part of DVB-IPI; this
tool exists to carry DVB-IPI streams over unmanaged or lossy networks with
SRT's ARQ-based recovery.
.PP
Exactly one of
.B \-i
(input) or
.B \-o
(output) must be an
.B srt://
URI, the other is a regular
.BR dipirec (1)-style
endpoint: RTP or plain UDP multicast, an HTTP(S) TS stream (source side
only), stdin/stdout, or a file. Only one direction is served per process.
.PP
An
.B srt://
endpoint address is either
.IB host : port
(calls out, caller) or
.BI @ host : port
(binds/listens/accepts, listener); the leading
.B @
mirrors this toolkit's own
.BR rtp://@ / udp://@
convention. Unlike RIST's fixed sender-calls-out/receiver-listens rule,
SRT's caller/listener role is independent of which side produces the
media \(em either
.B \-i
or
.B \-o
may carry the
.BR @ .
.IR host
is a numeric IP, not a hostname.
.PP
Repeating
.B \-i
or
.B \-o
with further
.B srt://
URIs bonds several links carrying the same stream, selected with
.B \-\-group\-mode
.RB ( broadcast
or
.BR backup ).
Every bonded peer of one endpoint must agree on caller vs. listener.
.PP
.B \-\-rendezvous
swaps the srt:// side's connection setup for SRT's rendezvous mode: both
ends actively dial each other, neither is a listener, which lets two hosts
behind separate NATs punch a direct hole to one another. It requires
.B \-\-local
and cannot combine with
.B srt://@
or
.BR \-\-group\-mode .
SRT's rendezvous only does the NAT hole\-punching itself \(em each side
still needs to learn the other's public address some other way first.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-in " " \fIuri\fR
Input endpoint. Repeatable if it is an
.B srt://
URI, to bond several links.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " " \fIuri\fR
Output endpoint. Repeatable if it is an
.B srt://
URI, to bond several links.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface " " \fIiface\fR
Interface for the non-SRT side's multicast join or send.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-insecure
Skip TLS verification. Only meaningful with an
.B \-i https://
source.
.TP
.B \-\-group\-mode \fImode\fR
.B broadcast
or
.BR backup .
Required when bonding (repeated
.B srt://
peers on one endpoint), rejected otherwise. Needs a
.B libsrt
built with bonding support
.RB ( ENABLE_BONDING=ON ,
off by default upstream and in most distro packages); this build rejects the flag outright
if its own linked libsrt lacks it.
.TP
.B \-\-rendezvous
Use SRT rendezvous instead of connect/listen. Requires
.BR \-\-local .
.TP
.B \-\-local \fIhost:port\fR
Local bind address for
.BR \-\-rendezvous .
.TP
.B \-\-passphrase \fIpw\fR
Encryption passphrase, 10 to 79 characters.
.TP
.B \-\-pbkeylen \fIn\fR
AES key length in bits:
.BR 16 ", " 24 ", or " 32 .
Only valid with
.BR \-\-passphrase ,
default
.B 16
when a passphrase is set.
.TP
.B \-\-streamid \fIid\fR
SRT stream id, passed to a listening peer on accept.
.TP
.B \-\-packetfilter \fIcfg\fR
Raw SRT packet filter configuration string, e.g.
.BR fec,cols:10,rows:5 .
Off by default, matching SRT's own default.
.TP
.B \-\-latency \fIms\fR
SRT latency in milliseconds. Default is the library default.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
Colorize log output:
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
or
.BR never .
Default
.BR auto .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics \fIpath\fR
Unix datagram socket path for metrics output. Default
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-id \fIname\fR
Stable instance id for metrics. Metrics are disabled unless this is set.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-interval \fIs\fR
Metrics snapshot interval in seconds. Default
.BR 5 .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print periodic bridge statistics on stderr.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipisrt \-i rtp://@239.1.1.1:5000 \-o srt://1.2.3.4:9000 \-\-latency 200
Sender: read an RTP multicast and send it over SRT to a listening receiver.
.TP
.B dipisrt \-i srt://@0.0.0.0:9000 \-o rtp://@239.1.1.1:5000
Receiver: listen for an incoming SRT connection and re-emit as RTP
multicast.
.TP
.B dipisrt \-i rtp://@239.1.1.1:5000 \-o srt://1.2.3.4:9000 \-o srt://5.6.7.8:9000 \-\-group\-mode broadcast
Bonded sender: the same stream carried over two independent SRT links.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
Non-zero on argument errors or I/O/network failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipirec (1),
.BR dipirist (1),
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipiradiohead (1)
.PP
